{% comment %}
  Raise the mega-menu height cap so the WOMEN panel fits without scrolling.

  The cap stays — an unbounded panel could run off a short screen with no way to
  reach the rest — it is just set higher. The theme's own value leaves too
  little room: measured live, the longest panel needs 587px at a 1000px window
  and 537px at 700px, while the theme allowed only 485px at 700px, so the last
  few CLOTHING links sat behind a scrollbar.

  100vh - 150px clears the header and announcement bar and still fits the
  longest panel down to roughly a 700px window. Below that the content genuinely
  cannot fit, and the cap correctly lets it scroll rather than spilling off
  screen.

  !important because the cap is declared on this same class, so a plain override
  would depend on which stylesheet loaded last.
{% endcomment %}

<style>
  .sub-menu.mega-menu-container,
  .mega-menu-container {
    max-height: calc(100vh - 150px) !important;
  }
</style>
